h moved, return `ErrConflict` as today.\n3. `worker/conflict.go` (new): `(l *Loop) conflictInput(ctx, role config.Role, n int, branch string, r reviewfix.Round) (f executor.File, mainTip string, ok bool, err error)`. Fetch `main` into a private ref in `RepoDir` (use `d.Git` and the loop's existing remote/token plumbing), resolve its SHA, trial-merge in a scratch worktree with `MergeNoCommit` and `MergeAbort`, and write `conflict.md`: starts with `agentjob.UntrustedHeader`, names the round, lists conflicted paths, includes both sides' summaries (hunks via `Git.FileAt`/diff, marked as untrusted text from the PR and from `main`), capped at `feedbackCap`. A clean trial merge (main moved) returns `ok=false`.\n4. `worker/feedback.go`, `worker/run.go` (input build around lines 108-125): when the newest requested round has `Reason == reviewfix.ReasonConflict`, add `conflict.md` (also in the untrusted list) instead of `review-feedback.md`. Add `mergeParent string` to the `job` struct. Before the agent step, run `MergeNoCommit(mainTip)` in the job worktree so the agent sees real conflict markers and `tests:` runs on the merge result.\n5. `worker/facts.go`, `worker/guard.go`, `worker/run.go` (`round`/`push`, `committer.CodeRequest` near line 570): in a conflict round, compute `facts` and the diff-guard line count relative to `jb.mergeParent` (the PR's own changes) instead of `BaseSHA`, so main's changes do not trip `diff_max_lines`. Refuse the round (needs-human, nothing pushed) if any `<<<<<<<`/`>>>>>>>` marker remains or `UnmergedPaths` is non-empty. Pass `MergeParent: jb.mergeParent` in the request. A non-done role file keeps ending needs-human through the existing path.\n6. `servecmd/merger.go`, `servecmd/reviewfix.go`, `servecmd/serve.go` (line ~486): build the reviewfix loop once and pass it as `Rounds` in `merger.Deps` (replace the \"deliberately unset\" comment). Keep the `reviewfix` loop registered as before. The issue also says \"starter config\": no conflict-round switch exists in config or in `initcmd` today (`Deps.Rounds` is the switch), and starter role files live under protected `.ard/` paths, so make no config or `initcmd` change unless the worker finds a real setting. If it does, note it on the PR.\n7. `docs/proposal.md` (lines ~160, ~332, ~378) and `docs/layout.md` if a file is listed there: replace the \"follow-up\" text with the conflict-round behaviour, add the worker conflict round and the merge-parent commit in the code lane. Update `committer` and `worker` `doc.go` comments if they describe the code lane or inputs.\n\n### Test plan\n\nTest command: `make test`, and `make lint`.\n\n- `gitx/merge_test.go` `TestMergeNoCommitConflict`: union conflict returns the path; `TestMergeNoCommitClean`: none; `TestUnmergedPathsAfterResolve`: empty; `TestMergeNoCommitOtherError`: bad ref errors.\n- `committer/code_test.go`: `TestCommitCodeMergeParent` (two parents, second is main tip, tree has resolved files and main's other files, lease push used); `TestCommitCodeMergeParentNotMainTip` (refused, nothing pushed); `TestCommitCodeMergeParentInvalid` (non-hex, with Create: `ErrInvalid`); `TestCommitCodeMergeLeftover` (unmerged path refused); `TestCommitCodeMergeForbiddenPath` (declared `.github/x` rejected by `CheckCodePath`); `TestCommitCodeMergeBranchMoved` (`ErrConflict`); `TestCommitCodeMergeNoLeaseNoForce` (assert the push args carry a lease and no force).\n- `worker/loop_test.go`: `TestConflictRoundInput` (header, listed untrusted, paths and hunks, capped, replaces `review-feedback.md`); `TestConflictRoundCleanMerge` (`ok=false`); `TestConflictRoundUnionResolved` (fake agent keeps both sides, push has `MergeParent`); `TestConflictRoundOverlapNeedsHuman`; `TestConflictMarkersLeftRefused`; `TestConflictRoundDiffGuardOwnChanges` (main adds lines beyond `diff_max_lines`, round passes; PR's own oversize changes still rejected).\n- `servecmd`: test that `mergerLoop` has `Rounds` set if existing wiring tests allow it.\n- End-to-end 