 no `-X`, using the existing `g.run` env scrubbing. Exit 1 with unmerged paths returns them (`diff --name-only -z --diff-filter=U`, NUL-split); exit 1 with none, or any other failure, is an error. Add `MergeAbort(ctx, dir)` and `ConflictHunks(ctx, dir, path)` which uses `--no-textconv --no-ext-diff` under the same empty attribute source. Do NOT add a post-agent `UnmergedPaths` for the agent's worktree (M2). Test in `gitx/merge_test.go` (new) with `gitx/gittest`.\n2. `gitx/write.go`: add `Parents []string` to `CommitOp` (extra parents beyond HEAD, optional). When set, build the commit with `git commit-tree <tree> -p HEAD -p <each>` (message from stdin) then `update-ref`/`reset --soft` to it, keeping hooks off and gpgsign off. Skip the `ErrNothingToCommit` check when `Parents` is set so a merge whose tree equals the branch tip is still committed (S5). Update the `Effects` implementation and the dry-run effect in `effects` so the logged op shows both parents. Test: two parents, tree-equal-to-tip merge commits.\n3. `committer/code.go`, `committer/committer.go`, `committer/errors.go`: add `MergeParent string` to `CodeRequest` (40-hex, optional, never with `Create`). `codeSnapshot` validates with `shaRe` (`ErrInvalid`), stores `snap.mergeParent`; more than `MaxFiles` (256) files stays `ErrInvalid`. New `ErrMergeParent` wrapping `ErrInvalid`. In merge mode the lane does NOT run `git merge`: fetch `+refs/heads/main` from `cfg.RemoteURL` into a new private ref (new `mergeRef` constant, not `upstreamRef(\"main\")`), and refuse unless it equals `MergeParent`; then `ResetHard` to `MergeParent`, apply the snapshot files over it with the existing write loop in `attempt`, run `StagedChanges` against `MergeParent`, and commit with `CommitOp.Parents = [MergeParent]` on top of a HEAD set to the fetched branch tip (so parents are `[branchTip, MergeParent]` in that order, built via commit-tree on the staged tree). Add an `attemptMerge` method beside `attempt` rather than branching inside it.\n4. `committer/guard.go`, `committer/committer.go` (`checkModes`): in merge mode `CheckStaged(declared, changes)` and `checkModes` use the changes relative to `MergeParent`, so an undeclared path differing from main is refused and a declared one must pass `CheckCodePath`; also run `CheckCodePath` on every path in `diff(MergeParent, result)`, including protected ones brought in or reverted. Declared files whose content equals main's drop out of the diff naturally. Push stays `ForceWithLease` on the fetched branch tip, never `--force`.\n5. `committer/committer.go` (`run`, lines ~241-291): in merge mode there is no retry. Re-fetch main on every attempt and recheck equality with `MergeParent`; if the branch moved (stale lease, non-fast-forward, or changed declared paths) return `ErrConflict` with no reapply (the existing loop reapplies, so skip it for `s.mergeParent != \"\"`). The commit message stays controller-built (`CodeMessage` + `Ard-Job`) with no agent or main text.\n6. `worker/conflict.go` (new): `(l *Loop) conflictInput(ctx, role config.Role, n int, branch string, r reviewfix.Round) (f executor.File, mainTip string, conflicted []string, ok bool, err error)`. Fetch `+refs/heads/main` from the remote URL into a private ref in `RepoDir`, resolve `mainTip` (this is the only source of `mergeParent`; never from role-file frontmatter or `conflict.md`). Trial-merge in a scratch worktree with `MergeNoCommit`, record the conflicted paths there, then `MergeAbort`. A clean merge returns `ok=false`. Write `conflict.md`: `agentjob.UntrustedHeader`, round, conflicted paths (cap path count and per-path bytes; escape names from the `-z` list; redact hunks with the existing secret redaction; the code fence is longer than any backtick run in the content; both sides marked untrusted), truncated on a UTF-8 boundary with `strings.ToValidUTF8` as in `worker/feedback.go:75`, within `feedbackCap` (S2).\n7. `worker/feedback.go`, `worker/run.go` (input build ~108-125): when the newest requested round has `Reason == reviewfix.ReasonConflict`, add `conflict.md` (also in the untrusted list) instead of `review-feedback.md`. Add `mergeParent string` and `conflicted []string` to `job`. Before the agent step, run `MergeNoCommit(mainTip)` in the job worktree (controller-run, hardened as in step 1) so the agent sees real markers. After the agent step run NO git command in the agent's worktree for conflict handling: read the recorded conflicted files through `os.Root` / the snapshot and run the advisory marker check there (≥7-char `<`, `=`, `>`, `|` marker lines, only in recorded conflicted paths; a hit ends needs-human, nothing pushed) (M2, S3). Enforcement is the committer's (steps 3-5).\n8. `worker/facts.go` (lines ~40-70), `worker/guard.go`, `worker/run.go` (`round`/`push`, `committer.CodeRequest`): in a conflict round compute `Changed`, `prLines` and the declared file list from `jb.mergeParent`/`mainTip` (replace `jb.cfg.SHA` and the `MergeBase` logic with `mainTip` as base), so only the PR's own changes count against `diff_max_lines` (S1). More than `MaxFiles` declared files ends needs-human. Pass `MergeParent: jb.mergeParent` in the request. A GitHub rejection of a merge that brings main's `.github/workflows` changes (App lacks the `workflows` permission) ends as needs-human with a clear comment, never a retry (S4).\n9. `reviewfix/loop.go` `mergeIncludes` (~387-399): also require that the second parent (`ps[1]`) is on main's first-parent history (new `gitx` helper or `git rev-list --first-parent` membership check against the fetched main), in addition to `IsAncestor(base, head)` (S6).\n10. `servecmd/merger.go`, `servecmd/reviewfix.go`, `servecmd/serve.go` (~486): build the reviewfix loop once, pass it as `Rounds` in `merger.Deps`, replacing the \"deliberately unset\" comment (this is part A's switch). No config or `initcmd`/starter-file change: none exists and starter files under `.ard/` are protected; if the worker finds a real setting it notes this on the PR.\n11. `docs/proposal.md` (~160, ~332, ~378) and `docs/layout.md` if it lists the new files: replace the \"follow-up\" text with the conflict round and the merge-parent commit; update `committer` and `worker` `doc.go` where they describe the code lane or inputs.\n\n### Test plan\n\nTest command: `make lint test`.\n\n- `gitx/merge_test.go`: `TestMergeNoCommitConflict` (returns path), `TestMergeNoCommitClean`, `TestMergeNoCommitOtherError` (bad ref), `TestMergeIgnoresAttributes` (branch `.gitattributes` `merge=union` or `conflict-marker-size` has no effect), `TestCommitParents` (two parents, order), `TestCommitParentsSameTree` (tree equals tip is committed).\n- `committer/code_test.go`: `TestCommitCodeMergeParent` (parents `[tip, main]`, tree = main plus declared, lease push, no force); `TestCommitCodeMergeParentNotMainTip` (refused, nothing pushed); `TestCommitCodeMergeParentInvalid` (non-hex, and with `Create`: `ErrInvalid`); `TestCommitCodeMergeUndeclaredDiffRefused` (a path differing from main not declared); `TestCommitCodeMergeProtectedBroughtIn` and `...Reverted` (`.github/`, `.ard/` path differs: refused); `TestCommitCodeMergeForbiddenDeclared` (`CheckCodePath` rejection); `TestCommitCodeMergeBranchMovedNoRetry` (`ErrConflict`, no reapply, one fetch-and-push attempt); `TestCommitCodeMergeMainMovedBetweenAttempts`; `TestCommitCodeMergeSameTreeAsTip`; `TestCommitCodeMergeOverMaxFiles`; `TestCommitCodeMergeNonLeasePush` (stub push without lease is refused).\n- `worker/loop_test.go`: `TestConflictRoundInput` (header, untrusted listing, replaces `review-feedback.md`, caps, escaped names, long backtick fence, UTF-8 truncation, redaction); `TestConflictRoundCleanMerge` (`ok=false`); `TestConflictRoundResolved` (fake agent resolves; request has `MergeParent` = fetched main tip, not from role-file frontmatter); `TestConflictMarkersLeftNeedsHuman`; `TestConflictRoundOverlapNeedsHuman`; `TestConflictRoundDiffGuardOwnChanges` (main adds lines beyond `diff_max_lines`: passes; PR's own oversize changes: rejected); `TestConflictRoundNoGitInAgentTree` (agent-planted `.git` config/clean filter never runs); `TestConflictWorkflowRejectedNeedsHuman`.\n- `reviewfix`: `TestMergeIncludesSecondParentOnMain` (second parent not on main's first-parent history: false).\n- `prgate` / merger: whitespace-only conflict resolution plus stale human approval is not covered (#366 cover must not treat the conflict merge as an update-branch merge).\n- `servecmd`: `merger.Deps.Rounds` is set, if existing wiring tests allow it.\n- End to end with the fakes (`merger/integration_test.go` or existing harness): conflicting PR, conflict round, worker resolves, code lane pushes merge with main as second parent, fake GitHub clears the conflict, reviewers re-run; second case with an overlapping edit ends `ard:needs-human`.\n\n### Risk\n\nHigh. Security-sensitive committer code: path guard, staged-change check, merge-parent verification, lease push, new commit-with-parents path, and the worker's trust of agent output. Mitigations are the single tree invariant enforced in the committer, no git in the agent's worktree after the agent step, a strict private-ref `MergeParent` with no merge-mode retry, and hardened merge flags. Public interfaces: `committer.CodeRequest`, `gitx.CommitOp`, `effects`, `gitx.Git`, `servecmd` wiring. No migration. No `merge.protected_paths` entry is edited. The switch turns on before the human-written worker prompt section lands unless that PR merges first or alongside.\n\n### Size\n\nL (about 1,400 to 2,200 changed lines with tests; may pass `diff_warn_lines` (2,000 when not set), so expect a large-change note, still under the 3,000 limit). Files touched: `internal/gitx/{merge.go (new),merge_test.go (new),write.go}`, `internal/effects/*` (commit op and dry-run), `internal/committer/{code.go,committer.go,guard.go,errors.go,code_test.go}`, `internal/worker/{conflict.go (new),feedback.go,run.go,facts.go,guard.go,loop_test.go}`, `internal/reviewfix/loop.go` (+test), `internal/servecmd/{merger.go,reviewfix.go,serve.go}`, `internal/merger/integration_test.go`, `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/layout.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":7,"newStart":8,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Tree invariant (governs steps 3-6).** Let `declared` be the worker's full diff against the fetched `mainTip` (not `BaseSHA`). The merge result must satisfy `diff(MergeParent, result) ⊆ declared`, and every path in that diff passes `CheckCodePath`. Outside the PR's own paths the result is main's tree, so `.github/`, `.ard/`, `.gitmodules`, `.gitattributes` are byte-identical to main."," ","-1. `gitx/merge.go` (new): `(g *Git) MergeNoCommit(ctx, dir, ref string) (conflicted []string, err error)`. Runs `git -c rerere.enabled=false -c merge.renormalize=false -c submodule.recurse=false -c core.autocrlf=false -c commit.gpgsign=false -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null merge --no-commit --no-ff --no-verify --no-edit -s ort <ref>` with `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE` set to the empty tree (`4b825dc642cb5e9ab4f9c4a2f3a8a3e9a3c0b8a` is wrong to hardcode: compute with `git hash-object -t tree /dev/null`), no `-X`, using the existing `g.run` env scrubbing. Exit 1 with unmerged paths returns them (`diff --name-only -z --diff-filter=U`, NUL-split); exit 1 with none, or any other failure, is an error. Add `MergeAbort(ctx, dir)` and `ConflictHunks(ctx, dir, path)` which uses `--no-textconv --no-ext-diff` under the same empty attribute source. Do NOT add a post-agent `UnmergedPaths` for the agent's worktree (M2). Test in `gitx/merge_test.go` (new) with `gitx/gittest`.","+1. `gitx/merge.go` (new): `(g *Git) MergeNoCommit(ctx, dir, ref string) (conflicted []string, err error)`. Runs `git -c rerere.enabled=false -c merge.renormalize=false -c submodule.recurse=false -c core.autocrlf=false -c commit.gpgsign=false -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null merge --no-commit --no-ff --no-verify --no-edit -s ort <ref>` with `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE` set to the empty tree (compute its id with `git hash-object -t tree /dev/null`; do not hardcode it), no `-X`, using the existing `g.run` env scrubbing. Exit 1 with unmerged paths returns them (`diff --name-only -z --diff-filter=U`, NUL-split); exit 1 with none, or any other failure, is an error. Add `MergeAbort(ctx, dir)` and `ConflictHunks(ctx, dir, path)` which uses `--no-textconv --no-ext-diff` under the same empty attribute source. Do NOT add a post-agent `UnmergedPaths` for the agent's worktree (M2). Test in `gitx/merge_test.go` (new) with `gitx/gittest`."," 2. `gitx/write.go`: add `Parents []string` to `CommitOp` (extra parents beyond HEAD, optional). When set, build the commit with `git commit-tree <tree> -p HEAD -p <each>` (message from stdin) then `update-ref`/`reset --soft` to it, keeping hooks off and gpgsign off. Skip the `ErrNothingToCommit` check when `Parents` is set so a merge whose tree equals the branch tip is still committed (S5). Update the `Effects` implementation and the dry-run effect in `effects` so the logged op shows both parents. Test: two parents, tree-equal-to-tip merge commits."," 3. `committer/code.go`, `committer/committer.go`, `committer/errors.go`: add `MergeParent string` to `CodeRequest` (40-hex, optional, never with `Create`). `codeSnapshot` validates with `shaRe` (`ErrInvalid`), stores `snap.mergeParent`; more than `MaxFiles` (256) files stays `ErrInvalid`. New `ErrMergeParent` wrapping `ErrInvalid`. In merge mode the lane does NOT run `git merge`: fetch `+refs/heads/main` from `cfg.RemoteURL` into a new private ref (new `mergeRef` constant, not `upstreamRef(\"main\")`), and refuse unless it equals `MergeParent`; then `ResetHard` to `MergeParent`, apply the snapshot files over it with the existing write loop in `attempt`, run `StagedChanges` against `MergeParent`, and commit with `CommitOp.Parents = [MergeParent]` on top of a HEAD set to the fetched branch tip (so parents are `[branchTip, MergeParent]` in that order, built via commit-tree on the staged tree). Add an `attemptMerge` method beside `attempt` rather than branching inside it."," 4. `committer/guard.go`, `committer/committer.go` (`checkModes`): in merge mode `CheckStaged(declared, changes)` and `checkModes` use the changes relative to `MergeParent`, so an undeclared path differing from main is refused and a declared one must pass `CheckCodePath`; also run `CheckCodePath` on every path in `diff(MergeParent, result)`, including protected ones brought in or reverted. Declared files whose content equals main's drop out of the diff naturally. Push stays `ForceWithLease` on the fetched branch tip, never `--force`."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K7tCSZksBELsUG599fpzXp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPMriC5Winn2cQkYT8iX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote the \"## Implementation\" section of `.ard/323/plan.md` to address the security review, and wrote `.ard/323/triage-engineer.md` with status done. Nothing was built or run; this is plan text only. #366 is now on main, so the earlier block no longer applies.\n\nThe plan now has 11 steps, a test plan, risk and size. Size is L (about 1,400 to 2,200 changed lines, possibly over the 2,000-line warning threshold) and risk is high. The main design points:\n\n- **Tree rule:** the committer enforces one invariant. The merge result may differ from main's tip only in the PR's declared paths, and each of those must pass `CheckCodePath`.\n- **Merge commit:** the committer does not run `git merge`. It resets to the merge parent, applies the snapshot, checks staged changes against it, and commits with the branch tip and merge parent as parents. `CommitOp` gains a parents field, so dry-run logs both.\n- **Merge parent:** it is fetched from the remote URL into a private ref and rechecked on every attempt. It comes only from the worker's own fetch, and merge mode has no retry.\n- **Worker:** it runs no git commands in the agent's worktree after the agent step. The diff guard is measured from main's tip. `conflict.md` has caps, escaping and redaction.\n- **Smaller items:** the plan also covers hardened merge flags, an advisory marker check, a clean stop to needs-human when GitHub rejects a workflow-file merge, and committing a merge whose tree equals the branch tip. It also requires the second parent to be on main's first-parent history in `reviewfix.mergeIncludes`, and the negative tests listed in the review.\n\nThe starter config is still left to a human because those files are protected. The worker prompt section for conflict rounds is also still a separate human PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":33397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"output_tokens":607,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72fa6700-2768-426f-a304-0498d8eb3f0c","uuid":"0d7c3c22-ffde-4e99-b899-eb67723ed1e8","timestamp":"2026-11-25T08:50:59.721Z","request_id":"req_011ChPMri4QFZ63AkamYF4aF"}
